                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 241</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On January 9, Senator Henry Cabot Lodge
                    sent a letter to the Department of State in which he expressed concern over the
                    military provisions of the Treaty of Peace with Italy and how these provisions
                    prohibited Italy’s rearmament. Lodge
                    called for some steps to “end the present highly unfortunate and unjust
                    situation” caused by the Peace Treaty. Senator Lodge’s letter and the Department’s response are printed in
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, March 5, 1951, page
                    379.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
